# Copy to .env for local development. Values match docker-compose.yml.
#
# FCP_DB_PORT moves the Postgres host port, for a machine that already has one
# on 5432. It must agree with the port in DATABASE_URL and TEST_DATABASE_URL.
# FCP_DB_PORT=5433
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://fcp:fcp@localhost:5432/fcp
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://fcp:fcp@localhost:5432/fcp_test

# ESPN_LEAGUE_ID is public. ESPN_SWID and ESPN_S2 are the cookies from a
# logged-in espn.com session (required for a private league) — treat those
# two as secrets.
ESPN_LEAGUE_ID=
ESPN_SWID=
ESPN_S2=

# ESPN_SEASON is optional and normally left unset. The season is derived from
# the date: ESPN labels a season by the year it ends in and turns over in
# October, so a schedule follows the rollover on its own. Set this only to pin
# a one-off backfill to a particular year. Pinning a *schedule* is how you end
# up refreshing a season that finished months ago while everything reports
# healthy.
# ESPN_SEASON=

# FCP_TRACKED_TEAM_ID is the ESPN team id the listener fetches news for on
# every status pass, and the one the digest reports on. Without it the passes
# still snapshot everyone, and the digest has no team so it does nothing.
# FCP_TRACKED_TEAM_ID=

# FCP_DIGEST_URL, FCP_DIGEST_CHAT_ID and FCP_TELEGRAM_BOT_URL were here until
# 2026-09-22 and no longer do anything. Everything goes by email now: a
# member's digest and his alerts, and the watchdog's notices to the operator.
# Leaving them set in an existing .env is harmless; delete them.

# Where everything is delivered (app/notify.py). Plain SMTP, so any
# transactional provider's endpoint works (Postmark, Resend, SES, Fastmail, a
# relay on the box). Configured when the host, the sender and at least one
# recipient are all set; FCP_EMAIL_TO takes several, comma separated, and is
# the operator's own inbox: the watchdog's notices go there. Port 465 is
# implicit TLS, anything else is STARTTLS; 587 is the submission port nearly
# every provider wants.
#
# FCP_EMAIL_FROM wants a stable display name that never changes -- "Full
# Court Press <fcp@your-domain>" -- because a From name that moves is a
# deliverability problem, not a style choice (docs/jobs.md).
#
# FCP_SMTP_PASSWORD belongs in this file on the VPS and nowhere else: not in
# a unit file, not in a shell history, not in the repository. It is never
# logged, never printed, and never part of an error message.
#
# Confirm the setup with: python scripts/notify_test.py
# FCP_EMAIL_TO=
# FCP_EMAIL_FROM=
# FCP_SMTP_HOST=
# FCP_SMTP_PORT=587
# FCP_SMTP_USER=
# FCP_SMTP_PASSWORD=
